# 06.07.2026

## What I worked on
Started the CI/CD task — needed GitHub Actions for lint, tests, build, and deploy to GitHub Pages.

## What I did
- Forked the repo and created branch `feature/ci-cd`
- Added three workflow files: validate on push to `feature/**`, PR checks, deploy to Pages
- Set `homepage` in package.json to `https://alima987.github.io/ci-cd`
- Opened PR #1 into `main`

## Where I got stuck
Not sure at first how deploy should work — the assignment says "GitHub Actions" as Pages source, not "Deploy from a branch". Also confused about `publicPath`: locally it's `/`, but on Pages the app lives under `/ci-cd/`.

## How I worked through it
Read the task page again and looked at how other RS School projects handle gh-pages. Added `base-path.ts` and `baseHref` in webpack so assets load from the right folder in production.

## Decisions made
- Used official `deploy-pages` action instead of pushing to `gh-pages` branch — seems like the current recommended way
- Branch name `feature/ci-cd` matches the assignment table, repo name is just coincidence

## Time spent
~3 h
